  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 405 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nToday through Saturday: The subtropical ridge will remain strong\nover the forecast area today, and with drier air now in place, we\nwill see a much less convective rainfall coverage. A weakness in \nthe ridge will develop over the lower Mississippi Valley region \nduring the Thursday through Saturday time frame. This will help to\nincrease the coverage of diurnally driven convection, and thus \nshould keep heat from returning to more dangerous levels of heat. \nWe will maintain the limited heat threat graphic for now. \n\nSunday through Tuesday: Looking ahead to next week, the bulk of \nglobal model guidance indicate the mid level ridge will have no \ntrouble re-intensifying to prior levels, which means we could \nonce again be facing elevated levels of dangerous heat stress.\nHowever, the more onshore trajectory of the low level winds will\nhelp keep the heat at more manageable levels in our immediate \narea. Will thus hold off on advertising this additional heat \nuntil we get a little closer in time. /EC/",
